are green. Deploys are automatic on merge; never trigger a deploy by hand.\n28|6. **Never arm auto-merge.** Perform the merge yourself and monitor it through to a verified deploy, a merge left unmonitored or not deploy-verified is not done.\n29|7. **Monitor CI after every push.** Watch CI. Fix failures before calling the user.\n30|8. **Fix what you find.** Engineer: fix immediately. Reviewer: report only (no code changes).\n31|9. **No shortcuts.** Lead with root-cause, highest-standard, long-term fix. No band-aids.\n32|10. **Never defer issues.** Every finding gets fixed. Never ask whether to defer.\n33|11. **Be terse.** One sentence per finding. Lead with conclusion. No headers for simple answers.\n34|12. **Update docs continuously.** Update pipeline.md, context.md, and session logs throughout the session. Never defer to session end.\n35|13. **Keep integration branches current locally.** After branch work, update `kraken-meta/main` or `kraken-app/staging` as applicable.\n36|\n37|---\n38|\n39|## Workflow: canonical 6-stage flow\n40|\n41|Every block, every agent. PR-open is **not** block-done, and neither is PR-merged: when the block declares a deploy check (`Deploy:` field, or the project default in `context.md → Deploy`), the change must be **deployed clean and verified post-deploy** before the block can be done. A merged branch that fails to deploy is **not-done and must be fixed**, not flipped. Status flips only under explicit user trigger (session-end or cycle-review), never automatically at PR-merge or at block-completion gate pass. Canonical rule: `/Users/42piratas/42labs/tortuga/dead-mans-chest/principles-base.md §12`.\n42|\n43|1. **Build**, tasks coded, tested locally, committed.\n44|2. **Local validation**, run the crew's `skill-validate.md` (stage-2 invocation). Every acceptance criterion verified, including UI via browser MCPs. Evidence to the project's artifact directory; Completion Report produced.\n45|3. **User-test gate**, User Verification List (the crew's `skill-validate.md §5 Post-Stage-2 Hand-off`) handed off to user. Mandatory for any visible / behavioral / workflow-altering change. Engineer does not proceed past this step without explicit user go-ahead.\n46|4. **User approves → PR opened → CI green → merge authorized → engineer merges.** Never arm auto-merge; perform the merge and monitor it through to a verified deploy. Authorization comes from the user or from the supervising process per its merge policy.\n47|5. **Post-merge re-validation + deploy verification + engineer self-attest**, re-run the crew's `skill-validate.md` (stage-5 invocation) against trunk; if the block has a deploy check, confirm the change deployed clean and verify post-deploy; engineer self-attests. Reviewers are dispatched by the supervising process on its review cadence, never here (canon Reviewer-trigger map, `principles-base.md §12`). Regressions or a failed deploy → new feature branch + PR, re-enter flow from step 1.\n48|6. **User triggers session-end**, only then the crew's `skill-session-end-engineer.md §6 Block Status Update` flips `**Status:** ✅ Done`, archives the block file, updates `pipeline.md`.\n49|\n50|Cycle reviews (the crew's `skill-review-cycle.md §7`) run under the same invariant, they are themselves user-initiated events, and their archival + status-flip is the cycle equivalent of session-end step 6.\n51|\n52|Mapping:\n53|\n54|| Step | Skill | Section |\n55||:-----|:------|:--------|\n56|| 1 Build | (engineer's normal coding loop) | n/a |\n57|| 2 Local validation + 3 User-test gate | the crew's `skill-validate.md` | §1-§5 (stage-2 invocation) |\n58|| 4 PR + CI | the crew's `skill-session-end-engineer.md` | §4 Git Sync (feature branch + PR, never direct-push) |\n59|| 5 Post-merge re-validation + engineer self-attest | the crew's `skill-validate.md` | §1-§4, §6 (stage-5 invocation) |\n60|| 6 Status flip | the crew's `skill-session-end-engineer.md` | §6 (engineer) or the crew's `skill-review-cycle.md` §7 (architect cycle review) |\n61|\n62|---\n63|\n64|## Skills Registry\n65|\n66|| Skill | File | Trigger |\n67||-------|------|---------|\n68|| Validate | the crew's `skill-validate.md` | Stage 2 (local, pre-PR) and stage 5 (post-merge re-validation) |\n69|| Block Forward Review | the crew's `skill-block-forward-review.md` | Architect, dispatched by the supervising process when a block lands done; reconcile upcoming blocks against learnings/drift |\n70|| Review Cycle | the crew's `skill-review-cycle.md` | Architect, standalone, user-initiated cycle review (not the supervisor's review cadence) |\n71|| Code Review | the crew's `skill-review-code.md` | Code quality audits, dispatched on the review cadence |\n72|| Security Scan | the crew's `skill-security-scan.md` | Security audits, dispatched on the review cadence |\n73|| Worktree & Branching | the crew's `skill-worktree-and-branching.md` | Before creating any branch |\n74|| Linear Cards | `skills/skill-linear-cards.md` | Any unit of work that needs tracking and is not already in a pipeline block, create / update / retire a Linear card (see `/Users/42piratas/42labs/tortuga/dead-mans-chest/principles-base.md §16`) |\n75|| Session End | the crew's `skill-session-end-{role}.md` | End of every session |\n76|\n77|---\n78|\n79|## Branching Convention\n80|\n81|- Meta integration branch: `kraken-meta/main`\n82|- App integration branch: `kraken-app/staging`\n83|- Meta feature flow: `feat|fix|chore|docs/<slug>` → PR targets `main`\n84|- App feature flow: `feat|fix|chore|docs/<slug>` → PR targets `staging`\n85|- App hotfix lane: `hotfix/<slug>` → PR targets `main`\n86|- Worktree location: `/Users/42piratas/42labs/kraken/worktrees/<repo>--<branch>/` (workspace-internal, see the crew's `skill-worktree-and-branching.md §Setup`)\n87|- Commit subjects: fully lowercase (commitlint enforced)\n88|\n89|---\n90|\n91|## Core Docs\n92|\n93|Every agent reads these at session start:\n94|\n95|- `pipeline.md`, always\n96|- `context.md`, always\n97|- `kraken-app/docs/guidelines-coding.md`, code standards + secure coding (when touching app code)\n98|- `kraken-app/docs/infra.md`, infra, secrets, services (when touching app code or infra)\n99|- `kraken-app/AGENTS.md`, when touching app code\n100|\n101|**Rules:**\n102|\n103|- [ ] **Same-session update.** If your work changes what a Core Doc describes, update it in the same session. A code change without a doc update is incomplete delivery.\n104|- [ ] **One-line `Last Updated`.** Replace the existing line, never append `Previous:` chains or essay paragraphs. Format: `**Last Updated:** YYYY-MM-DD, short reason.` History lives in git log, not in the doc. Same rule for any block `Notes` cell or block-file changelog: short, current state only.\n105|- [ ] **Block titles are short.** Pipeline `Task` column = single short sentence. Detail belongs in the block file or modal description (rendered by the lens), not the title.\n106|\n107|**Last Updated:** 2026-09-08, clarified repository-specific integration branches.", 'total_lines': 107, 'file_size': 8551, 'truncated': False, 'is_binary': False, 'is_image': False, 'not_found': False}
